'''Stordan Tonc''', nicknamed "'''Stordie''',"<ref name="Helmet Collection">{{HelmetCollectionCite|62|Weapons & Uniforms}}</ref> was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] [[Rebel trooper|soldier]] that served in the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] as a [[corporal]] during the [[Galactic Civil War]]. He joined the rebels after an [[Uprising on Qemia 7|uprising]] on<ref name="Visual Guide">''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]''</ref> his [[homeworld]]<ref name="Birth of Rebellion" /> of [[Qemia 7]].<ref name="Visual Guide" /> During the war's first battle, the [[Battle of Scarif]], Tonc became a member of [[Rogue One]]. Tonc stayed with the [[shuttle]] along with several [[Special Forces Trackers Unit|Pathfinders]] and the defected [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] cargo [[pilot]] [[Bodhi Rook]]. When the Imperials finally arrived to the same pad as the [[Starship|shuttle]], Tonc and his men filed out and defended the vessel. When Bodhi tried to connect the shuttle to the [[Citadel Tower|communications tower]] Tonc tried to cover him, but was shot down. Although he was [[Death|killed]], his sacrifice was not in vain as Bodhi was successfully able to contact the ''[[Profundity]]'' and told them to take down the [[Shield Gate]]. Bodhi was killed shorty after by a [[grenade]] thrown by a [[Coastal defender stormtrooper|Shoretrooper]].<ref name="Rogue One" />

{{Char-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Stordan Tonc, albeit unidentified, was portrayed by [[Jordan Stephens]] in the [[2016]] [[Star Wars Anthology Series|''Star Wars'' Anthology]] film ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''.<ref name="Rogue One" /> The character later received their name in [[Dorling Kindersley]] 2016 reference book ''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]''.<ref name="Visual Guide" /> According to Stephens, the actor was asked to appear for one scene as Tonc in the [[Disney+]] live-action series ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'', though unsure which season. However, a week prior to the shoot, Stephen was asked to cut their hair&mdash;[[Wikipedia:Dreadlocks|dreadlocks]] that had been grown for six years&mdash;which the actor refused. Stephen tried to compromise by suggesting a helmet to hide their hair, though it was denied, cancelling Tonc's return altogether.<ref name="Andor">{{TikTok|jordanfstephens|video/7475812395395386646|[[Jordan Stephens]]|description=🔫🔫🔫|date=2025-02-27|archivedate=20250228122933}}</ref>

